WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:16.282
SHOW ONLY THE EPBS LAYER
In the Explorer, ⊞ on EPBS scopes every diagram to the end-product breakdown: one configuration item per thing procured, built or delivered.

2
00:00:16.282 --> 00:00:27.826
GENERAL VIEW
Sixteen configuration items, each drawn with its fielded usage, its contract and its verification case. Too small to read whole, so pick one.

3
00:00:27.826 --> 00:00:41.278
READ ONE ITEM
Select BatteryPack, press Selection. Around it: its contract, its verification case and a hazard. Properties lists its «Trace» with SwarmMember, the PA part it realises.

4
00:00:41.278 --> 00:00:53.060
INTERCONNECTION VIEW
No wiring at this level: 16 item definitions and their 16 fielded usages. Counts sit on the usages: select batteryPacks, Multiplicity 24.

5
00:00:53.060 --> 00:01:06.256
REQUIREMENT VIEW
Each fielded usage satisfies its item's contract, as storeForwardSoftware does ReportStoreForwardSoftwareContract. Before recording we deleted one of these links.

6
00:01:06.256 --> 00:01:19.376
A CONTRACT ON ITS OWN
BatteryPackContract is now satisfied by nothing. Its text: at least 40 minutes of flight, a swap in no more than 20 minutes, at least two qualified sources.

7
00:01:19.376 --> 00:01:30.782
DRAW A SATISFY LINK
Pick Satisfy in the palette, then click the fielded usage first: batteryPacks, which now satisfies only the battery-supplier hazard.

8
00:01:30.782 --> 00:01:42.125
THEN CLICK THE CONTRACT
Then click the contract it satisfies, BatteryPackContract. The link is created and selected, and the diagram is laid out again.

9
00:01:42.125 --> 00:01:53.994
THE RESULT
batteryPacks satisfies BatteryPackContract again. The file gets the same line back, satisfy BatteryPackContract by batteryPacks, at the end of EPBS.

10
00:01:53.994 --> 00:02:07.522
PARAMETRIC VIEW
48 constraints: each contract's assume and require, with its condition written in the box, and each verification's objective, which only names the contract it verifies.

11
00:02:07.522 --> 00:02:20.589
READ ONE CONTRACT'S CONDITIONS
Zoomed in, the first pair: DroneAirframeContract assumes a full charge at the start, and requires at least 40 minutes of flight and 18 m/s cruise.

12
00:02:20.589 --> 00:02:33.385
CASE VIEW
The verification cases, one per contract. Each is drawn with its subject, the item under test, and its objective, which in the text names the contract it verifies.

13
00:02:33.385 --> 00:02:45.789
READ ONE CASE
VerifyBatteryPack: a discharge test for endurance, a timed swap at the recharge point and an audit of sources. Its subject, pack, is the item under test.

14
00:02:45.789 --> 00:02:58.296
TREE VIEW
What EPBS contains, one branch at a time. Select BatteryPackContract: +4 on its box opens its subject pack, its id and its two constraints, assume and require.
